  "nl_text": "The rschema_0078 database is designed to store information about authors and their articles. The database contains four tables: Author, Article, Author_creates_article, and Author_modifies_article. The Author table stores details about each author, including their ID, email, gender, introduction, name, and phone number. The Article table stores information about each article, including its ID, collection volume, comment volume, content, like volume, reading volume, title, creation time, last modification and save author ID, last modification and save time, and total number of words in the article. The Last_modification_and_save_author_ID column in the Article table references the Author table, establishing a relationship between authors and the articles they last modified and saved. The Author_creates_article table stores information about which authors are responsible for creating articles, including the article ID, author ID, author order, author responsible for part, and author role, with the primary key being a composite of the article ID and author ID. The Author_modifies_article table stores information about which authors have modified articles, including the article ID, author ID, modify notes, modify save time, and modify start time, with the primary key being a composite of the article ID, author ID, and modify save time. The Author_creates_article and Author_modifies_article tables both reference the Article and Author tables, establishing relationships between authors and the articles they create and modify.",
  "gold_question": "The article management system manages multiple articles. Each article has an article ID, article title, article content, creation time, total number of words, article reading volume, article like volume, article collection volume, article comment volume, the time of the last modification and save, and the author ID of the last modification and save. The system also manages multiple authors. Each author has an author ID, name, gender, phone number, email address, and introduction. Each article can be created by multiple authors, and the author order, responsible part, and role of each author are recorded. Authors can modify articles, and each modification records the modification start time, modification save time, and modification notes. The system ensures the accuracy of article content and the transparency of author contributions by recording article creation and modification information.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0078.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0078\nCREATE TABLE `author` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `introduction` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `article` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `collection_volume` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `comment_volume` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `like_volume` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reading_volume` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `last_modification_and_save_author_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_modification_and_save_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_words` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `article_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`last_modification_and_save_author_id`) REFERENCES `author` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `author_creates_article` (\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `author_order` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `author_responsible_for_part` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `author_role` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`article_id`, `author_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `author_creates_article_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`article_id`) REFERENCES `article` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `author_creates_article_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `author` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `author_modifies_article` (\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `modify_notes` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `modify_save_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `modify_start_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`article_id`, `author_id`, `modify_save_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `author_modifies_article_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`article_id`) REFERENCES `article` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `author_modifies_article_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `author` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
